  "native_campaign_supported": false,
  "coverage_limit": "One run records Clang/LLVM source coverage of the yaml extension (yaml.c, parse.c, detect.c; emit.c and the headers report 0) and of source-built libyaml 0.2.5 (api.c, reader.c, scanner.c, parser.c) for one yaml_parse() call on a valid control. PHP itself is a plain build and is not covered; the PHP tree walk in summary.php runs no extension or libyaml code. AFL++ feedback comes from the native overlay: pecl/yaml yaml.c, parse.c and detect.c plus libyaml 0.2.5 reader.c, scanner.c and parser.c, instrumented through an allowlist while the same harness runs; the PHP runtime, emit.c and the rest of libyaml add no AFL++ tuples, and the full-harness maps equal the parse-only fuzz-target maps. The pinned base image does not bundle php-fuzzer; replay is per case.",
  "fuzz_smoke_entrypoint": "/opt/php/bin/php",
