  "underlying_coverage_subject_prefix": "/work/source/yaml-0.2.5/",
  "underlying_format_specific_coverage_file_suffix": "/yaml-0.2.5/src/parser.c",
  "afl_overlay": "fuzzing/afl-native/yaml/php/pecl_yaml",
  "scope": "One YAML document from local bytes passed to the documented yaml_parse(string $input, int $pos = 0, int &$ndocs = ?, array $callbacks = null): mixed with a YAML_MAP_TAG callback that casts each mapping to stdClass; ext/yaml applies callbacks to implicit tags too, so mappings return as stdClass in source order and sequences as PHP lists, which the harness walks into the shared exact typed tree (map/seq/str/int/float/bool/null, aliases expanded) with node counts and maximum depth. The harness requires ndocs = 1.",
  "observable_limits": "ext/yaml resolves plain scalars with YAML 1.1 rules in detect.c (yes/no/on/off booleans, 0x/0o/0b and sexagesimal numbers, timestamps); the controls avoid every such scalar. Without the YAML_MAP_TAG callback mappings are PHP arrays and {} cannot be told from []. Integer-like mapping keys become PHP int array keys before the cast; the controls have none. Tags, merge keys, multi-document streams, yaml_parse_file/yaml_parse_url, the yaml.decode_* ini settings and malformed input are not exercised.",
